codex
The spherical run regressed to `7.88e-05`, and it exposed a design bug in the earlier LHS construction: each half-design coordinate was restricted to the same lower Gaussian half, so whitening had been repairing a strongly correlated orthant cloud. I’m fixing the antithetic LHS properly by choosing the lower/upper member of every complementary stratum pair independently per coordinate, then applying only the now-small covariance whitening. This should be the largest remaining gain.
